tps://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/114316","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114316","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114316.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114316.patch","merged_at":"2026-02-18T18:11:04Z"},"body":"Follow-up to https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106218\r\n\r\nI decided to split https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109645 into several smaller PRs, starting with iOS ~~and visionOS.~~ (EDIT: not entirely sure this PR supports visionOS)\r\nThis PR adds support for SDL3 joystick input driver for the rest of the supported Apple platforms.\r\n\r\nAlso, it would be nice if someone could test if `Input.has_joy_light()` and `Input.set_joy_light()` work on iOS ~~and visionOS~~ with this PR. :D\r\nI think they're supposed to work since `JoystickSetLED` function is implemented in the MFI joystick driver and a check for iOS version is included inside:\r\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/63227bbc8ae5300319f14f8253c8158b846f355b/thirdparty/sdl/joystick/apple/SDL_mfijoystick.m#L1452-L1473\r\n\r\nTODO:\r\n- [x] Rebase\r\n- [x] Check if joypad LED works (Sorry, I can't check myself :( ) (it does)\r\n- [x] Check if joypad motion sensors work (Sorry, I can't check myself :( ) (at the moment, they don't)\r\n- [x] Include bruvzg's SDL code fix\r\n- [x] Documentation\r\n- ~~Report SDL not detecting controller motion sensors on iOS~~\r\n- [x] Return true for `Input.has_joy_motion_sensors()` if only one of the motion sensors is available \r\n- [x] Document `Input.get_joy_accelerometer()` and `Input.get_joy_gravity()` being unsupported on iOS due to OS limitations.","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/follower